{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1 — PROVEN, runtime-confirmed)\n\n**Problem.** The `tickets` branch commit rate jumped ~10x since 2026-08-23; ~88% is the enrichment quartet (ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH + TICKET_DIGEST). 1,239 tickets were re-enriched ~15x each.\n\n**Why a single ticket is re-enriched ~15x (the mechanism).** The digest sidecar is keyed by a content hash over `title + description + comment bodies` (`overlap/digest_sidecar.py::_normalize_text` / `content_hash`, and `freshness` compares stored hash vs current). The drain's self-heal `enrich_drain._stale_digest_ids` (src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:158) scans **every** ticket dir on **every** drain and returns **every** ticket whose digest is `present-stale`; `_collect_claims` then re-enqueues each with `soak_min=0, now_ns=now-1` (immediately claimable), with **no idempotence, debounce, or per-ticket cap**. So each external content drift (a comment, an edit, or a reconcile writeback) invalidates the digest and produces exactly one full enrich cycle. ~15 drifts/ticket over 8 days ≈ ~2/day of ordinary churn on active tickets — no tight infinite loop, an **unbounded-per-drift** loop.\n\n**Feedback-loop question — answered.** Enrichment's OWN writes do NOT re-stale the digest: `enrich()` (src/rebar/llm/enrich.py) writes no ticket comment; the TICKET_DIGEST sidecar and the ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE queue events are reducer-IGNORED (not in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES`), so they never enter compiled `comments`/`description` and are excluded from `content_hash`. There is therefore no self-sustaining enrichment→digest loop. The drift is **external** (comment/edit churn + reconcile writebacks).\n\n**Why the drift became unbounded GROWTH.** Correctness fix `be8a0c0` (Gerrit 989, bug 8185-2d4b-d2bf-4282) removed the only growth bound — `_prune_queue_events` (kept only the newest queue event/ticket) and digest `prune(keep=1)` — deliberately, because physical deletion of committed UUID events breaks the append-only union-merge invariant across stale clones. Before `be8a0c0`, the self-heal still re-fired on drift, but pruning capped the live tree to ~1-2 files/ticket. After it, every re-fire's 4 events are retained forever. Re-firing × removed-pruning = the fan-out.\n\n**Runtime proof (discriminating).** Repro (`repro_fanout.py`, offline `_DigestRunner`): one first-time enrich, then N=12 content drifts each followed by a drain →\n```\nfirst-time drain processed=1\ndrifts=12  re-enrichment cycles=12\nENQUEUE=13 CLAIM=13 DONE=13 DIGEST=13  quartet-total=52\n```\n12 drifts → 12 re-enrichment cycles (1:1, unbounded) → 13 of each quartet event retained, none pruned. This is the exact production signature (1,239 tickets × ~15 drifts × 4 events ≈ the ~81K quartet events). Discriminates against the \"enrichment self-loop\" hypothesis (ruled out above) and the \"single infinite tight loop\" hypothesis (ratio is 1 cycle per external drift, not runaway).\n\n**Defect origin / attribution.** The unbounded *growth* (reported symptom) was introduced by `be8a0c0059571b340cd7705191769a4a64998643d` — `rebar-ticket 8185-2d4b-d2bf-4282` (git blame of the removed `_prune_queue_events`/`prune` is unambiguous; `be8a0c0` is the introducing commit, not a carrier). `be8a0c0` knowingly created the retention problem and deferred the merge-safe replacement to follow-up epic 4520 (apparent-sighted-cockatoo), which was never built. Class = `plan_defect` (the plan removed the sole bound and shipped without a replacement). `caused_by 8185` recorded.\n\n**Legitimacy = defect.** Cited authority: epic 4520 states removing pruning \"creates a deliberate long-term retention problem\" to be bounded; the downstream disk-fill incident (5a05) is corroborating operational harm. Unbounded store growth violates the store's operational-cost invariant. Re-enriching on genuine drift is legitimate; doing so **without any bound** is the defect.\n\n**Fix (prevention, this ticket).** A per-ticket re-enrichment **debounce** on the self-heal path: skip a present-stale ticket whose latest `DONE_ENRICH` is younger than `overlap_reenrich_debounce_min` (default 24h). Bounds re-firing to ≤1 cycle/ticket/window; deletes no event (preserves the union-merge invariant `be8a0c0` protects). Minimal-yet-sufficient: it stops the fan-out at its multiplier without disabling first-time or post-window enrichment."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788035352340904828,"uuid":"1d5ee157-ef90-47ee-8985-9553482d5ce8"}